# Normalize text files to LF on checkin, regardless of the OS they were
# authored on. Keeps compose files, scripts, and configs diff-friendly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary types -- never touch line endings, just to be safe on top of
# git's own content-based auto-detection.
*.png -text
*.PNG -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.svg -text
*.deb -text
*.ico -text

# d2 diagrams are left exactly as originally authored -- do not renormalize
*.d2 -text

# MISTAKES.md only grows at the end, from many branches at once: union merge keeps both sides' new
# entries instead of conflicting (kaywoz, 2026-11-26). Applies to local git merges and rebases; GitHub's
# web merge may not use it (unverified), so a PR can still show a conflict until main is merged locally.
MISTAKES.md merge=union
